# AI Engineering Rules

- Treat LLM output as untrusted input.
- Validate model output before using it in business logic.
- Prefer structured outputs for machine-consumed responses.
- Never hardcode model API keys.
- Keep provider credentials in environment variables.
- Handle model errors, rate limits, and timeouts.
- Keep retrieval, business logic, and generation responsibilities separate.
- Preserve source metadata in RAG systems.
- Do not assume model output is factually correct.
- Avoid sending sensitive data to external models unnecessarily.
- Keep prompts clear, versioned, and maintainable.
